not medicated for these symptoms.
Additional history obtained at presentation indicated that
many of the episodes of weakness were triggered by strong
emotions such as excitement, anger, or laughter. He experi-
enced weakness most of the time, with occasional periods of
normal power lasting up to 30 minutes. He had a history of
chronic daytime sleepiness over the past 4 months with fre-
